Cleanup: redirect/security.txt regression tests + edge-policy audit doc

- tests/test_cloudflare_policy.py gains three regression tests:
  - test_security_and_locale_security_redirect_to_trust extracts the
    /security/ rule from the worker source and simulates it in Python:
    /security, /security/, /de/security/, /fr/security must 301 to the
    matching /trust/ route - never the /app//api fallback that would send
    them to /contact-us/, never a 404 fallthrough; the rule must also
    precede the contact rule and the ASSETS fetch, must not over-match
    (/securityx/, /security/extra, /trust/), and the portable
    marketing/_redirects mapping must document the same behaviour.
  - test_legacy_domain_redirects_to_canonical: getassureai.com (and www)
    answers 301 to the https://assureproof.com canonical host with path
    and query kept and the http upgrade in the same hop; its docstring
    now matches exactly what it asserts.
  - test_security_txt_expires_is_valid_future_date: Expires must parse as
    an aware UTC datetime, be at least 30 days in the future (checked
    against marketing/security.txt and the dist copy) and within a year,
    so the file cannot silently expire.
- docs/bot-policy-audit.md: new current-state audit grounded in the
  worker source and live curl checks (security.txt is 200 with
  Contact/Expires/Canonical - the old 404 claim is gone; getassureai
  consolidates in one hop - the no-redirect claim is gone). Dashboard-
  only items are marked [UNREADABLE / CONFIRM IN DASHBOARD] (Bot Fight
  Mode, AI Crawl Control, WAF rate-limit rule, zone redirect rule);
  [CONFIRM] items and counsel-gated legal text are untouched.
- docs/runbooks/ship-webpage.md: stale Resend addresses corrected to the
  current assureproof.com inboxes (matching SALES_INBOX/EMAIL_FROM in the
  worker), legacy-path gotcha now mentions the /security -> /trust/ move.

Local: bash marketing/build.sh (144 pages) + pytest tests/ = 99 passed.
